WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:07.189
The rest of Barry's training went smoothly—until late in the day when he suddenly spun around and bumped into Ally.

2
00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.957
"Whoa!" she cried as she stumbled forward, a platter of meteor fries slipping from her grasp.

3
00:00:12.958 --> 00:00:18.112
Without thinking, Ally activated her levitation powers, sending the plate floating in midair.

4
00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:21.678
The customers inside the diner broke into applause.

5
00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:27.955
"We got to see one of those famous tricks that Gourmet Greta wrote about!" one customer said.

6
00:00:27.956 --> 00:00:35.696
"We're so lucky!" said another. "I heard she doesn't do the tricks very often."

7
00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:43.512
Ally bowed as if she'd done it all on purpose and then delivered the fries.

8
00:00:43.513 --> 00:00:48.232
Barry hurried after her as she headed for the counter.

9
00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:54.026
"That was amazing! When are you going to teach me how to do that trick?" he asked eagerly.

10
00:00:54.027 --> 00:00:58.935
"Never!" Ally thought. But she forced herself to smile patiently at him.

11
00:00:58.936 --> 00:01:01.596
"After you've been here for a while," she said.

12
00:01:01.597 --> 00:01:05.884
"There's still a lot you have to learn about the menu and other stuff."

13
00:01:05.885 --> 00:01:10.081
"I'm a fast learner," Barry said. "Teach me now!"

14
00:01:10.082 --> 00:01:16.502
Luckily, before she had to reply, a customer at table five waved at Barry. "Excuse me! Waiter?"

15
00:01:16.503 --> 00:01:20.863
"Looks like table five needs you, Barry," Ally said.

16
00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:25.530
While Barry hurried over to his table, Ally ducked into the kitchen.

17
00:01:25.531 --> 00:01:32.429
"Yikes," she thought, blowing out a breath. "Barry is so persistent!"

18
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.838
At the end of the day, Ray made a meal for all the workers.

19
00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:42.005
Ally, Randy, Ray, and Barry sat down in a booth to eat together.

20
00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:48.572
"This is delicious," Barry said, biting into his club sandwich. "What's your secret, Ray?"

21
00:01:48.573 --> 00:01:54.039
"Ray uses only the freshest ingredients," Randy said.

22
00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.464
"Not that." Barry shook his head.

23
00:01:56.465 --> 00:02:00.841
"How did you get Gourmet Greta to come and review the diner? Did you bribe her?"

24
00:02:00.842 --> 00:02:05.709
"What?" Ray growled. "I'd never do something like that!"

25
00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:11.361
Barry threw his hands up and forced a laugh. "I was just kidding!

26
00:02:11.362 --> 00:02:15.079
I only meant that restaurant owners are always trying to get Greta to review them.

27
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.420
How did you manage it?"

28
00:02:18.421 --> 00:02:25.191
"She probably heard about how delicious his food is," Ally said loyally.

29
00:02:25.192 --> 00:02:29.293
"Yeah, that makes sense," Barry said. "I'm sure you're right."

30
00:02:29.294 --> 00:02:35.400
He gushed for a few minutes about Ray's cooking, but Ally couldn't tell if Barry actually meant what he was saying.

31
00:02:35.401 --> 00:02:38.788
Something about Barry was beginning to strike her as odd.

32
00:02:38.789 --> 00:02:41.594
Still, she'd been on Earth for only a little while.

33
00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:45.189
There was a lot she still didn't understand about human behavior.

34
00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.794
Barry ate another bite of his sandwich and then looked at his watch.

35
00:02:48.795 --> 00:02:55.672
"I've got to get home. My . . . father is expecting me," he added quickly.

36
00:02:55.673 --> 00:03:01.577
"See you tomorrow." And with that, he raced out of the diner.

37
00:03:01.578 --> 00:03:05.578
Randy scratched his head. "He's an odd one."

38
00:03:05.579 --> 00:03:10.132
Ally nodded. "I hope we didn't make a mistake by hiring him."

39
00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:16.082
Ray shrugged. "You were odd at first too, Ally," he said, laughing.

40
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:26.321
"I was, wasn't I?" Ally grinned. "And look how great I worked out!"

41
00:03:26.322 --> 00:03:29.190
Later Ally returned to her pod in the park.

42
00:03:29.191 --> 00:03:35.295
She took off her meld medallion and reverted to her Astralian form.

43
00:03:35.296 --> 00:03:41.030
"Ahh." She stretched. "That feels so much better."

44
00:03:41.031 --> 00:03:45.795
As Ally sat down at the control panel, the computer whirled to life.

45
00:03:45.796 --> 00:03:52.072
"Scanning the area. And detecting no new parts or fuel cells in the immediate vicinity."

46
00:03:52.073 --> 00:03:59.052
Ally sighed. "Bad news, Alpha. I couldn't find them. I'll have to search again tomorrow."

47
00:03:59.053 --> 00:04:01.958
"Searching is unnecessary," the computer said.

48
00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:07.618
"I have computed the exact location of the fuel cells and parts required to repair this pod."

49
00:04:07.619 --> 00:04:13.324
"What?" Ally cried. "That's fabulous news! Where are they?"

50
00:04:13.325 --> 00:04:15.806
The computer spat out a printout.

51
00:04:15.807 --> 00:04:19.610
Ally grabbed it. But her face quickly fell.

52
00:04:19.611 --> 00:04:24.638
"The parts are in the Sandville UFO Museum?" She groaned.

53
00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:28.392
"That can't be right, Alpha. I went there this morning.

54
00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:33.498
They don't sell anything we need in the gift shop."

55
00:04:33.499 --> 00:04:36.788
"The items are not in the gift shop," the computer said.

56
00:04:36.789 --> 00:04:40.367
"They are located in the museum's northeast quadrant."

57
00:04:40.368 --> 00:04:41.739
"Huh?"

58
00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:48.584
The computer printed out another document. This one showed a map of the museum.

59
00:04:48.585 --> 00:04:53.531
Ally studied it closely and then let out an even louder groan.

60
00:04:53.532 --> 00:05:00.370
"I know this location—it's Dr. Lloyd's office!"

61
00:05:00.371 --> 00:05:06.519
She jumped to her feet and started pacing around the pod. She thought as hard as she could.

62
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:19.952
But there was only one option: she'd have to go to Dr. Lloyd's opening on Friday.

